IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — THE SCHEDULES AS DATA: Tables A and B
-- (First Schedule paras 1-2, and Fifth Schedule Part 3 paras 1-2, which print
-- the same tables), the Second Schedule's conditions and periods, the Third
-- Schedule's classes (as `Third Schedule class` in wica-types.l4), the Fourth
-- Schedule's percentages, and the Sixth Schedule's laws.
--
-- The tables were GENERATED from ../source/WICA2019.txt by a script that read
-- each row and checked that the Fifth Schedule's tables equal the First's
-- (53 rows each, ages "14 and below" to "66 and above"); see NOTES.md.

§ `The Schedules`

§§ `Tables A and B — the multiplying factor by age on next birthday`

@ref Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 First Schedule para 1(1) Table A; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 1(1) Table A (identical)
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table A factor for age` age MEANS
    --       age on next birthday               factor
    BRANCH
        IF age AT MOST 14                    THEN 136
        IF age EQUALS 15                     THEN 135
        IF age EQUALS 16                     THEN 135
        IF age EQUALS 17                     THEN 134
        IF age EQUALS 18                     THEN 134
        IF age EQUALS 19                     THEN 133
        IF age EQUALS 20                     THEN 132
        IF age EQUALS 21                     THEN 132
        IF age EQUALS 22                     THEN 131
        IF age EQUALS 23                     THEN 130
        IF age EQUALS 24                     THEN 129
        IF age EQUALS 25                     THEN 128
        IF age EQUALS 26                     THEN 127
        IF age EQUALS 27                     THEN 127
        IF age EQUALS 28                     THEN 125
        IF age EQUALS 29                     THEN 124
        IF age EQUALS 30                     THEN 123
        IF age EQUALS 31                     THEN 122
        IF age EQUALS 32                     THEN 121
        IF age EQUALS 33                     THEN 120
        IF age EQUALS 34                     THEN 118
        IF age EQUALS 35                     THEN 117
        IF age EQUALS 36                     THEN 115
        IF age EQUALS 37                     THEN 114
        IF age EQUALS 38                     THEN 112
        IF age EQUALS 39                     THEN 110
        IF age EQUALS 40                     THEN 108
        IF age EQUALS 41                     THEN 107
        IF age EQUALS 42                     THEN 106
        IF age EQUALS 43                     THEN 105
        IF age EQUALS 44                     THEN 104
        IF age EQUALS 45                     THEN 103
        IF age EQUALS 46                     THEN 102
        IF age EQUALS 47                     THEN 101
        IF age EQUALS 48                     THEN 100
        IF age EQUALS 49                     THEN 98
        IF age EQUALS 50                     THEN 96
        IF age EQUALS 51                     THEN 94
        IF age EQUALS 52                     THEN 92
        IF age EQUALS 53                     THEN 90
        IF age EQUALS 54                     THEN 88
        IF age EQUALS 55                     THEN 86
        IF age EQUALS 56                     THEN 84
        IF age EQUALS 57                     THEN 82
        IF age EQUALS 58                     THEN 80
        IF age EQUALS 59                     THEN 78
        IF age EQUALS 60                     THEN 75
        IF age EQUALS 61                     THEN 72
        IF age EQUALS 62                     THEN 68
        IF age EQUALS 63                     THEN 63
        IF age EQUALS 64                     THEN 58
        IF age EQUALS 65                     THEN 53
        OTHERWISE                            48      -- 66 and above

@ref Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 First Schedule para 2(a) Table B; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 2(a) Table B (identical)
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table B factor for age` age MEANS
    --       age on next birthday               factor
    BRANCH
        IF age AT MOST 14                    THEN 181
        IF age EQUALS 15                     THEN 180
        IF age EQUALS 16                     THEN 179
        IF age EQUALS 17                     THEN 178
        IF age EQUALS 18                     THEN 178
        IF age EQUALS 19                     THEN 177
        IF age EQUALS 20                     THEN 176
        IF age EQUALS 21                     THEN 175
        IF age EQUALS 22                     THEN 174
        IF age EQUALS 23                     THEN 173
        IF age EQUALS 24                     THEN 172
        IF age EQUALS 25                     THEN 170
        IF age EQUALS 26                     THEN 169
        IF age EQUALS 27                     THEN 168
        IF age EQUALS 28                     THEN 167
        IF age EQUALS 29                     THEN 165
        IF age EQUALS 30                     THEN 164
        IF age EQUALS 31                     THEN 162
        IF age EQUALS 32                     THEN 160
        IF age EQUALS 33                     THEN 159
        IF age EQUALS 34                     THEN 157
        IF age EQUALS 35                     THEN 155
        IF age EQUALS 36                     THEN 153
        IF age EQUALS 37                     THEN 151
        IF age EQUALS 38                     THEN 149
        IF age EQUALS 39                     THEN 146
        IF age EQUALS 40                     THEN 144
        IF age EQUALS 41                     THEN 142
        IF age EQUALS 42                     THEN 140
        IF age EQUALS 43                     THEN 138
        IF age EQUALS 44                     THEN 136
        IF age EQUALS 45                     THEN 134
        IF age EQUALS 46                     THEN 132
        IF age EQUALS 47                     THEN 130
        IF age EQUALS 48                     THEN 128
        IF age EQUALS 49                     THEN 126
        IF age EQUALS 50                     THEN 124
        IF age EQUALS 51                     THEN 122
        IF age EQUALS 52                     THEN 120
        IF age EQUALS 53                     THEN 118
        IF age EQUALS 54                     THEN 116
        IF age EQUALS 55                     THEN 114
        IF age EQUALS 56                     THEN 111
        IF age EQUALS 57                     THEN 108
        IF age EQUALS 58                     THEN 105
        IF age EQUALS 59                     THEN 102
        IF age EQUALS 60                     THEN 99
        IF age EQUALS 61                     THEN 96
        IF age EQUALS 62                     THEN 92
        IF age EQUALS 63                     THEN 87
        IF age EQUALS 64                     THEN 82
        IF age EQUALS 65                     THEN 77
        OTHERWISE                            72      -- 66 and above

-- "according to the age on the next birthday of the [worker] at the time of
-- the accident": the completed years at the accident, plus one.
@ref First Schedule paras 1(1), 2(a)
GIVEN born     IS A DATE
      accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age on the next birthday, if born on` born `, at an accident on` accident MEANS
    `completed years` PLUS 1
    WHERE
        `completed years` MEANS
            IF    DATE_MONTH accident GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH born
               OR (DATE_MONTH accident EQUALS DATE_MONTH born AND DATE_DAY accident AT LEAST DATE_DAY born)
            THEN DATE_YEAR accident MINUS DATE_YEAR born
            ELSE DATE_YEAR accident MINUS DATE_YEAR born MINUS 1

§§ `Second Schedule — occupational diseases`

-- First column (condition) and third column (period). The second column
-- ("Any occupation involving exposure to …") decides whether the worker was
-- in a specified occupation: an input. As amended by G.N. No. S 751/2025 wef
-- 1 December 2025; the earlier Schedule is not in the source.
DECLARE `Second Schedule row` HAS
    `condition`          IS A STRING
    `period in months`   IS A NUMBER

@ref Second Schedule
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Second Schedule row`
`the Second Schedule row` item MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF item EQUALS 1  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Barotrauma", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 2  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Cataract due to infra-red, ultraviolet or ionising radiation", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 3  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Compressed air illness or its sequelae, including dysbaric osteonecrosis", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 4  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Diseases caused by excessive heat", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 5  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Diseases caused by ionising radiation", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 6  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Noise-induced hearing loss", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 7  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by aniline", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 8  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by arsenic", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 9  THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by benzene or a homologue of benzene", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 10 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by beryllium", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 11 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by cadmium", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 12 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by carbamates", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 13 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by carbon disulphide", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 14 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by carbon monoxide gas", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 15 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by cyanide", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 16 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by halogen derivatives of hydrocarbon compounds", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 17 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by hydrogen sulphide", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 18 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by lead", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 19 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by manganese", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 20 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by mercury", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 21 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by organophosphates", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 22 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by oxides of nitrogen", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 23 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Poisoning by phosphorus", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 24 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Toxic anaemia", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 25 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Toxic hepatitis", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 26 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Anthrax", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 27 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Glanders", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 28 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Leptospirosis or its sequelae", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 29 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Occupational infectious disease", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 30 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Work-related musculoskeletal disorder", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 31 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Asbestosis", 36)
        IF item EQUALS 32 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Byssinosis", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 33 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Occupational asthma", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 34 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Silicosis", 36)
        IF item EQUALS 35 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Occupational skin disease", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 36 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Malignant mesothelioma", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 37 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Occupational liver angiosarcoma", 12)
        IF item EQUALS 38 THEN JUST (`Second Schedule row` OF "Occupational skin cancer", 12)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Fourth Schedule — injuries deemed to result in permanent incapacity`

@ref Fourth Schedule
GIVEN i IS A `Fourth Schedule injury`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Fourth Schedule percentage for` i MEANS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `loss of 2 limbs`                                            THEN 100
    WHEN `loss of both hands or of all fingers and both thumbs`       THEN 100
    WHEN `loss of both feet`                                          THEN 100
    WHEN `total loss of sight`                                        THEN 100
    WHEN `total paralysis`                                            THEN 100
    WHEN `injuries resulting in being permanently bedridden`          THEN 100
    WHEN `any other injury causing permanent total incapacity`        THEN 100
    WHEN `loss of arm at shoulder`                                    THEN 75
    WHEN `loss of arm between elbow and shoulder`                     THEN 75
    WHEN `loss of arm at elbow`                                       THEN 75
    WHEN `loss of arm between wrist and elbow`                        THEN 70
    WHEN `loss of hand at wrist`                                      THEN 70
    WHEN `loss of 4 fingers and thumb of one hand`                    THEN 70
    WHEN `loss of 4 fingers`                                          THEN 60
    WHEN `loss of thumb, both phalanges`                              THEN 30
    WHEN `loss of thumb, one phalanx`                                 THEN 20
    WHEN `loss of index finger, 3 phalanges`                          THEN 14
    WHEN `loss of index finger, 2 phalanges`                          THEN 11
    WHEN `loss of index finger, one phalanx`                          THEN 9
    WHEN `loss of middle finger, 3 phalanges`                         THEN 12
    WHEN `loss of middle finger, 2 phalanges`                         THEN 9
    WHEN `loss of middle finger, one phalanx`                         THEN 7
    WHEN `loss of ring finger, 3 phalanges`                           THEN 7
    WHEN `loss of ring finger, 2 phalanges`                           THEN 6
    WHEN `loss of ring finger, one phalanx`                           THEN 5
    WHEN `loss of little finger, 3 phalanges`                         THEN 7
    WHEN `loss of little finger, 2 phalanges`                         THEN 6
    WHEN `loss of little finger, one phalanx`                         THEN 5
    WHEN `loss of first or second metacarpal (additional)`            THEN 8
    WHEN `loss of third, fourth or fifth metacarpal (additional)`     THEN 3
    WHEN `loss of leg at or above knee`                               THEN 75
    WHEN `loss of leg below knee`                                     THEN 65
    WHEN `loss of foot`                                               THEN 55
    WHEN `loss of all toes of one foot`                               THEN 20
    WHEN `loss of great toe, both phalanges`                          THEN 14
    WHEN `loss of great toe, one phalanx`                             THEN 3
    WHEN `loss of a toe other than the great toe, more than one lost` THEN 3
    WHEN `loss of sight of one eye`                                   THEN 50
    WHEN `loss of hearing, one ear`                                   THEN 30
    WHEN `total loss of hearing`                                      THEN 60

-- Note 2: "Where there is loss of 2 or more parts of the hand, the
-- percentage is not to be more than the loss of the whole hand" — loss of
-- the hand at the wrist, 70. Item 2 (both hands) is two hands, not a part
-- of one, and is not listed.
-- FORK F7: Note 2 speaks of "the hand"; the caller's list does not say which
-- hand each part was on, so all the parts listed are read as parts of one
-- hand. Losses on both hands are two calls, added by the caller.
@ref Fourth Schedule Note 2
GIVEN i IS A `Fourth Schedule injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a part of the hand:` i IF
    elem i (LIST
        `loss of 4 fingers and thumb of one hand`,
        `loss of 4 fingers`,
        `loss of thumb, both phalanges`,
        `loss of thumb, one phalanx`,
        `loss of index finger, 3 phalanges`,
        `loss of index finger, 2 phalanges`,
        `loss of index finger, one phalanx`,
        `loss of middle finger, 3 phalanges`,
        `loss of middle finger, 2 phalanges`,
        `loss of middle finger, one phalanx`,
        `loss of ring finger, 3 phalanges`,
        `loss of ring finger, 2 phalanges`,
        `loss of ring finger, one phalanx`,
        `loss of little finger, 3 phalanges`,
        `loss of little finger, 2 phalanges`,
        `loss of little finger, one phalanx`,
        `loss of first or second metacarpal (additional)`,
        `loss of third, fourth or fifth metacarpal (additional)`,
        `loss of hand at wrist`)

@ref Fourth Schedule items 1-26 and Notes 1-2
GIVEN injuries IS A LIST OF `Fourth Schedule injury`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Fourth Schedule percentage for the injuries` injuries MEANS
    IF   `capped` GREATER THAN 100 THEN 100 ELSE `capped`
    WHERE
        `hand parts` MEANS filter (GIVEN i YIELD `a part of the hand:` i) injuries
        `others`     MEANS filter (GIVEN i YIELD NOT `a part of the hand:` i) injuries
        `hand total` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the Fourth Schedule percentage for` i) `hand parts`)
        `hand`       MEANS IF count `hand parts` AT LEAST 2 AND `hand total` GREATER THAN 70 THEN 70 ELSE `hand total`   -- Note 2
        `capped`     MEANS `hand` PLUS sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the Fourth Schedule percentage for` i) `others`)

-- Note 1, "Total permanent loss of the use of a member is to be treated as
-- loss of that member", is applied by the caller choosing the injury.
-- Note 3 (loss of a remaining arm, leg or eye) is in wica-compensation.l4.

§§ `Sixth Schedule — laws for s 34D(2)`

@ref Sixth Schedule Part 1
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Sixth Schedule Part 1 — laws on the platform worker's use of vehicles` MEANS
    LIST "Active Mobility Act 2017 — Section 23D(1) or 28B(1)", "Road Traffic Act 1961 — Section 35(1) or 47G(1)"

@ref Sixth Schedule Part 2
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Sixth Schedule Part 2 — laws on the vehicle used` MEANS
    LIST "Active Mobility Act 2017 — Section 19", "Road Traffic Act 1961 — Any rules relating to the construction and equipment of vehicles made pursuant to section 6"
